Add a feature test macro to isaac.c which enables a special test mode.

In that mode, if a seed of 1024 zero-bytes is used, the contents of some
internal variables are verified to contain certain well-known intermediate
values.

A diagnostic message will be written to standard error at that point.

--- isaac-crc_2767905519.c	2026-02-10 05:37:46.148424483 +0000
+++ isaac.c	2026-02-10 04:02:52.967291525 +0000
@@ -17,6 +17,20 @@
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <assert.h>
 
+#if 0
+   /* Add special verification code.
+   |*
+   |* If a seed of all-zero bytes is detected, the program will verify that
+   |* certain known intermediate values match after 10 rounds. A diagnostic
+   |* message will then be written to stderr. The output written to stdout
+   |* will not change if this test is successful. Otherwise, the program
+   |* will abort with an error message.
+   |*
+   |* See FSE 1996 Conference paper (LNCS 1039) page 46 for details about
+   \* the well-known values for an all-zero seed. */
+   #define ZEROTEST
+#endif
